"""
LED WALL LEAD MACHINE
A VS Code-ready Streamlit app for finding LED wall sales leads, storing them in SQLite,
generating cold call scripts/emails, and tracking outreach in real time.

WHAT IT DOES
- Searches Google Places for prospects in target cities/categories
- Stores leads in a local SQLite CRM database
- Generates LED-wall-specific cold call scripts and outreach emails
- Lets you update lead status, notes, priority, and follow-up date
- Exports leads to CSV
- Provides a real-time Streamlit dashboard

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO BY DEFAULT
- It does not mass-call people automatically
- It does not mass-email people automatically
- It does not scrape private/personal data

SETUP
1. Create a folder in VS Code, e.g. led-lead-machine
2. Save this file as: led_wall_lead_machine.py
3. Create a .env file in the same folder with:

   GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_places_api_key_here
   SALES_EMAIL=citysaleslive@gmail.com
   SMTP_SERVER=smtp.gmail.com
   SMTP_PORT=587
   SMTP_PASSWORD=your_gmail_app_password_here

4. Install dependencies:

   pip install streamlit requests python-dotenv pandas

5. Run:

   streamlit run led_wall_lead_machine.py

NOTE: For Gmail, enable 2FA and generate an app-specific password at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords

NOTES
- You need Google Places API enabled in Google Cloud.
- Cold outreach must comply with CAN-SPAM, TCPA, DNC rules, platform policies, and local law.
- Use this to build qualified business leads and outreach drafts, not spam.
"""

